From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Draven <dravengarden@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:05:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Offer predicted prompts to Cowboy when its Provider opts in

The adapter predicts the next prompt after a completed turn only for
JetBrains AIR clients and publishes it as
`session_info_update._meta.promptSuggestions`. Cowboy offers exactly
that form in its composer, but it is not AIR, and the ACP schema its
worker reads has no `prompt_suggestions_update`. Its Codex Provider
package sets COWBOY_CODEX_PROMPT_SUGGESTIONS=1 to take the same
prediction; a managed call never predicts, and upstream's
CODEX_ACP_PROMPT_SUGGESTIONS=false still turns it off.

Cowboy-Delta: cowboy-prompt-suggestions
Upstream: cowboy-specific
Drop-When: Cowboy's worker reads ACP prompt_suggestions_update and codex-acp publishes it to clients advertising session.promptSuggestions
Tests: src/__tests__/CodexACPAgent/cowboy-prompt-suggestions.test.ts

diff --git a/src/CodexAcpServer.ts b/src/CodexAcpServer.ts
